</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:55:22-08:00","id":1037517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037481#post1037481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Summon a Fae from Arcadia</li> <li>Offer to trade a person and/or soul in exchange for power</li> <li>???</li> <li>Profit! [warning: captive may return as a vengeful Changeling or similar entity a few stories down the line if your ST has any sense]</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>oh i don't think that could be it, the book states you can only summon fae when you're gnosis 3 no mage just Awakening would have that experience","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:58:29-08:00","id":1037519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037487#post1037487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're poking around in the part of the Supernal that defines history and destiny as part of potentially attaining symbolic root access to those forces. Shit can go wrong in a fashion not unlike metaphorical enslavement to the things that determine what you can and can't accomplish, magically described in the forms of capricious fairies.</div> </div> </div> </div>is it a metaphor for misusing the fate arcanum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:58:47-08:00","id":1037520,"title":"","content":"I don't know anything about Mage but I thought that Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia were two different places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:02:17-08:00","id":1037522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037519#post1037519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it a metaphor for misusing the fate arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like a metaphor for any Acanthus who are Unwise enough to think that just because they <i>can </i>warp destiny, they <i>should </i>do so. Causality can bite back hard when poked enough, and mages are usually the only ones with sticks big enough to poke it that much in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037520#post1037520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know anything about Mage but I thought that Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia were two different places.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. The developers decided that the benefits of having a consistent answer outweighs the benefits of having a fungible one. They just happen to draw on similar sources for their motifs. In fact, Mage Arcadia is only a &quot;place&quot; in the sense that an internet page or the contents of a book is a &quot;place&quot;. It's a collection of abstract concepts that mages recognize as symbols, not somewhere you can walk to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-24-2017, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:06:13-08:00","id":1037527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037519#post1037519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it a metaphor for misusing the fate arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a metaphor for how making a misstep in a scenario that stands to give you some of the more broadly-applicable freedoms magic can provide is a good way to wind up with no magic powers and also Fucking Cursed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:21:08-08:00","id":1037572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037520#post1037520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know anything about Mage but I thought that Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia were two different places.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. They use the same name, Fae, but mage boils them down to the Moirae of Fate, and the Anachronisms of Time. <br /> <br /> Mages don't start with the book, all sorts of weird things can happen during your Awakening, mages can do a lot of things during them that they might not do otherwise. Or that they would <i>totally </i>do otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T22:04:51-08:00","id":1037666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037487#post1037487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're poking around in the part of the Supernal that defines history and destiny as part of potentially attaining symbolic root access to those forces. Shit can go wrong in a fashion not unlike metaphorical enslavement to the things that determine what you can and can't accomplish, magically described in the forms of capricious fairies.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a really fun descriptor. Way more fun to have Supernal beings mucking about with your life in subtle ways than just overtly enslaving you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T22:49:56-08:00","id":1037680,"title":"","content":"That paragraph opens with, &quot;Arcadia's fairy lords are <b>living forces of destiny</b>. ... you'll trade your destiny for theirs.&quot;<br /> <br /> The entire point of an Acanthus' Awakening is that they get to subvert destiny. That's their freedom and enlightenment: they write their own story. That's what it means to mess with the Fate Arcanum. And if they have to sacrifice someone else, to enslave them to a destiny that person didn't choose, to do it?<br /> <br /> That makes them a little worse than the rest.<br /> <br /> (And if you go up two paragraphs, you get &quot;These Mysteries ... [drown] failed Acanthus in the consequences of old lives rejected and new ones never fully lived. Unless [the prospective Acanthus] chase[s] the truth [of their freedom] they'll [...] penetrate the hidden world just enough <b>to enslave themselves to its monsters</b>&quot;. This is what it means to be Acanthus. It means that all of these possibilities are <i>your choice</i>, not just what-ifs. A mortal might be paralyzed by indecision at the prospect, or frozen into a predestined path they have no choice in, but the Acanthus can <i>always choose</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":2758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","user":"Errol216","date":". 01-25-2017, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:04:38-08:00","id":1037793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037680#post1037680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That paragraph opens with, &amp;quot;Arcadia's fairy lords are <b>living forces of destiny</b>. ... you'll trade your destiny for theirs.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The entire point of an Acanthus' Awakening is that they get to subvert destiny. That's their freedom and enlightenment: they write their own story. That's what it means to mess with the Fate Arcanum. And if they have to sacrifice someone else, to enslave them to a destiny that person didn't choose, to do it?<br /> <br /> That makes them a little worse than the rest.<br /> <br /> (And if you go up two paragraphs, you get &amp;quot;These Mysteries ... [drown] failed Acanthus in the consequences of old lives rejected and new ones never fully lived. Unless [the prospective Acanthus] chase[s] the truth [of their freedom] they'll [...] penetrate the hidden world just enough <b>to enslave themselves to its monsters</b>&amp;quot;. This is what it means to be Acanthus. It means that all of these possibilities are <i>your choice</i>, not just what-ifs. A mortal might be paralyzed by indecision at the prospect, or frozen into a predestined path they have no choice in, but the Acanthus can <i>always choose</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes Sense, thought I must admit I still don't fully get it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T09:48:38-08:00","id":1037884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037463-something-has-been-bugging-about-arcadia?p=1037522#post1037522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. The developers decided that the benefits of having a consistent answer outweighs the benefits of having a fungible one. They just happen to draw on similar sources for their motifs. In fact, Mage Arcadia is only a &quot;place&quot; in the sense that an internet page or the contents of a book is a &quot;place&quot;. It's a collection of abstract concepts that mages recognize as symbols, not somewhere you can walk to.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it was probably for the best to keep the two separated but even so, in my games the two will be the same, although the Watchtower of Arcadia is, to say the least, difficult to reach for pretty much anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}